 "text": "This tiny light is a trap. A real anglerfish, nearly a kilometer down. It waits on the seafloor with a fishing rod on its head. Swim too close, and you're dinner. Every spring off Japan, millions of firefly squid flash electric blue, turning the black water into a starfield. This Atolla jellyfish has a burglar alarm. Attack it, and it flashes a ring of blue light that calls in bigger predators. The vampire squid doesn't drink blood. When it's threatened, it releases a cloud of glowing mucus, and vanishes. On some nights, the glow even reaches the shore. Down there, three out of four animals make their own light. The deep sea isn't dark. It's glowing.",
